{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":5,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1509457891,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOkxhYmVsZWRFdmVudDEzMTg3ODIwMzQ="},"added":["enhancement"],"removed":[]},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1509458841,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM0MDc3Mjk2Ng==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1945#issuecomment-340772966"},"message":"I happen to create plugins for specific things from time to time. It literally takes me seconds to do one. It takes MUUUUCHH longer to create a command. Just check how many files you need to edit to get it running. Then you need to anticipate future complaints who much your new command increased the import time of datalad. Then you need to come up with parameter specs. Then you need to obey the order of args to not have the test fail. Then you need to be careful to not inflate the core API with your special needs/interest.\n\nIf someone makes commands as easy as plugins -- great! For now I am good with plugins.\n\nSee #1887 for the only aspect where I personally see the need for action. But until we can test datalad in a clean config there is no point in doing that, because none of the devs will actually use it for anything.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1509460529,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM0MDc4MTYxOQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1945#issuecomment-340781619"},"message":"I am talking primarily about possibility of exposing plugins as datalad \"commands\".  We should retain the ease of their creation/definition and discovery. If e.g. we could simply provide handler for argparse to react to \"unknown\" command, we could just do plugins discovery then, and react appropriately \n\n- include list of plugins into `datalad --help`\n- output plugins doc if `datalad PLUGIN --help`\n- parse arguments and run the plugin if `datalad PLUGIN --kwargs args`","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1521531434,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDM3NDUwMjU0MA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1945#issuecomment-374502540"},"message":"No longer an issue.","files":null},{"type":4,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1521531434,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDExOkNsb3NlZEV2ZW50MTUzMDIzODk0Ng=="},"status":2}]}